{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011Cd9yUAqKjY2PZVbSv7tFU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019Dztf1QJqsmcpw1bL16AsT","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"W2: build /livres list UI","prompt":"You are workstream W2 building the book list page of \"Ma Bibliothèque\", a French-language personal library app. Work ONLY inside /Users/tom/Documents/my-library/app (Next.js 16 App Router, src dir, Tailwind v4, shadcn/ui radix-nova style, TypeScript strict).\n\n## Context — read these files FIRST (frozen contracts, DO NOT MODIFY):\n- src/db/schema.ts (types Book, Author, BookWithAuthor)\n- src/lib/validation.ts (CATEGORIES, AUDIENCES, WORLDVIEWS, WORLDVIEW_LABELS, PERIODS, bookQuerySchema)\n- src/lib/normalize.ts (normalizeKey for accent-insensitive comparisons, formatYear)\n- src/lib/queries.ts (listBooks, getFilterOptions — call these from server components only)\n- src/app/layout.tsx and src/components/main-nav.tsx (layout shell, do not touch)\n- Also read app/AGENTS.md: this Next.js version has breaking changes; `params`/`searchParams` in pages are Promises you must await. Consult node_modules/next/dist/docs/ if unsure.\n\nThe SQLite db at data/library.db currently has a small fixture (5 authors / 8 books); later it will hold 1,000+ books, so the table must stay performant (no per-row heavy components; simple rows are fine, virtualization NOT required).\n\n## Your deliverables\n1. REPLACE the placeholder src/app/livres/page.tsx with a server component (keep `export const dynamic = \"force-dynamic\"`) that loads ALL books via listBooks() and filter option values via getFilterOptions(), then renders a client component `BooksView`.\n2. Create client components under src/components/books/ (this is YOUR directory namespace; do not create files outside it except the page above):\n   - books-view.tsx — top-level client component managing toolbar state, URL-synced via useRouter/useSearchParams (replace, no scroll). State in URL: search, filters, sort, view mode, groupBy.\n   - book-table.tsx — TanStack Table (@tanstack/react-table is installed) listing: Titre, Auteur, Catégorie, Genre, Période, Public (audience), Vision du monde, Année. Rows link to /livres/[id] (title cell is a Link; also whole-row click). Multi-sort: shift-click on headers (enableMultiSort), sortable columns with ArrowUpDown icons. Sorting must be accent-insensitive (use normalizeKey in sortingFns).\n   - book-filters.tsx — toolbar: accent-insensitive search input (matches title OR author name via normalizeKey, client-side), multi-select filter popovers (Popover + Command, checkbox items) for: Catégorie, Genre, Période, Public, Vision du monde, Courant. Each active filter shows count badge on its trigger; selected values render as removable Badge chips below the toolbar; a \"Réinitialiser\" button clears everything. Also preset sort combos in a Select: \"Titre A→Z\", \"Auteur A→Z\", \"Période (ancienne → récente)\", \"Année (récente → ancienne)\". Période order must follow the PERIODS array order, NOT alphabetical.\n   - book-grouped.tsx — grouped view: Accordion sections with group name + count badge, books listed inside as compact rows linking to detail.\n   - View toggle \"Tableau | Groupé\" (Tabs or ToggleGroup) plus a \"Grouper par\" Select shown in Groupé mode with options: Auteur, Genre, Période, Catégorie, Public, Vision du monde.\n3. Filtering/search/grouping all happen client-side over the full dataset passed from the server (the dataset is a few thousand rows max — fine). Multi-select filters combine as OR within a filter and AND across filters.\n4. French UI throughout: empty state \"Aucun livre ne correspond aux critères\", counts \"N livres\", audience labels capitalized (enfants→Enfants...), worldview displayed via WORLDVIEW_LABELS but keep chips short (capitalize the raw value, e.g. \"Cynique\"). Null fields display as \"—\".\n5. A button/link \"Ajouter un livre\" (top right of the page) linking to /livres/nouveau.\n6. Design: professional, dense but airy; shadcn components from src/components/ui (button, input, badge, select, popover, command, table, accordion, tabs, checkbox, separator, skeleton...). Muted foreground for secondary text. Sticky table header. Works in dark mode (semantic tokens only, no hardcoded colors).\n\n## Constraints\n- DO NOT modify: src/db/*, src/lib/*, src/app/layout.tsx, src/components/main-nav.tsx, src/components/ui/* (except adding new shadcn components via `npx shadcn@latest add -y <name>` if you need one that's missing), package.json deps (everything you need is installed), next.config.ts, any file under src/app/auteurs or src/app/api or src/app/livres/[id] or src/app/livres/nouveau (other agents own those; they may not exist yet — that's fine, just link to the routes).\n- Verify with `cd /Users/tom/Documents/my-library/app && npx tsc --noEmit` (must pass with zero errors in YOUR files) and `npx eslint src/app/livres/page.tsx src/components/books --max-warnings=0` if eslint works. DO NOT run `npm run build` or `npm run dev` (other agents share the directory).\n- Keep the git tree additive: do not commit; do not delete other files.\n\nReport back: files created/changed, tsc result, and any deviation from this spec."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4471,"cache_read_input_tokens":98106,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4471},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"893f4819-6d94-4f67-849d-3e57eeca4b35","uuid":"bd5d8d5a-7700-42e2-9de0-5e5bc8e878c9","timestamp":"2026-07-18T18:13:12.154Z","request_id":"req_011Cd9yU53ZnKDRF6aPFKgx2"}
