{"type":"system","subtype":"task_started","task_id":"aef356610bed9d794","tool_use_id":"toolu_01GtMpSuwmtsjsqUwu9ZNPnJ","description":"W3: book detail, CRUD, api/books","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_type":"local_agent","prompt":"You are workstream W3 building book detail + CRUD + the books API of \"Ma Bibliothèque\", a French-language personal library app. Work ONLY inside /Users/tom/Documents/my-library/app (Next.js 16 App Router, src dir, Tailwind v4, shadcn/ui radix-nova style, TypeScript strict).\n\n## Context — read these files FIRST (frozen contracts, DO NOT MODIFY):\n- src/db/schema.ts + src/db/index.ts (drizzle db, tables authors/books/analysisJobs, types)\n- src/lib/validation.ts (bookInputSchema with authorId-OR-newAuthor refine, bookUpdateSchema, authorInputSchema, bookQuerySchema, enums CATEGORIES/AUDIENCES/WORLDVIEWS/WORLDVIEW_LABELS/PERIODS)\n- src/lib/normalize.ts (normalizeText, normalizeKey, formatYear, formatLifespan)\n- src/lib/queries.ts (listBooks, getBook, listAuthors, countBooksByAuthor)\n- app/AGENTS.md: this Next.js version has breaking changes; `params` in pages AND route handlers are Promises you must await (`const { id } = await params`). Consult node_modules/next/dist/docs/ if unsure.\n\nFixture data: data/library.db has 5 authors / 8 books.\n\n## Your deliverables\n\n### A. API route handlers (zod-validated, French error messages, JSON always)\n- src/app/api/books/route.ts:\n  - GET: parse query params with bookQuerySchema (400 {error, details} on invalid), return {books: listBooks(query)}.\n  - POST: body validated with bookInputSchema. If newAuthor given (and no authorId): create the author first (name normalized via normalizeText, nameNormalized via normalizeKey; if an author with same nameNormalized already exists, REUSE it instead of erroring). Insert book (titleNormalized computed; updatedAt handled). 201 {book} (with author joined). 409 {error:\"Ce livre existe déjà pour cet auteur\"} on the (titleNormalized, authorId) unique violation. 400 if authorId references a missing author.\n- src/app/api/books/[id]/route.ts:\n  - GET → {book} via getBook, 404 {error:\"Livre introuvable\"}.\n  - PUT: bookUpdateSchema; same newAuthor handling; update updatedAt; 200 {book}; 404; 409 on unique violation.\n  - DELETE → delete the book (analysis_jobs rows cascade), 200 {ok:true}; 404 if missing.\n- HTTP status codes exactly as above. Wrap unique-constraint detection on the SQLite error message (\"UNIQUE\").\n\n### B. Pages (French UI)\n- src/app/livres/[id]/page.tsx — server component (`export const dynamic = \"force-dynamic\"`), getBook(Number(id)), notFound() if absent. Layout: title + author line (author name links to /auteurs/[id]), badge row (Catégorie, Genre, Période, Public, Vision du monde via WORLDVIEW_LABELS, Courant, Thème — only non-null ones), metadata card (Année de publication, Langue originale, enriched flag shown as badge \"Ajouté par Claude\" when true), Notes section if present. Buttons: \"Modifier\" → /livres/[id]/modifier, \"Supprimer\" opens an AlertDialog (client component src/components/books/delete-book-dialog.tsx) that calls DELETE /api/books/[id], toasts success via sonner, router.push(\"/livres\"). Also render `<AnalysisPanel book={...} author={...} />` from \"@/components/books/analysis-panel\".\n- src/components/books/analysis-panel.tsx — create a STUB ONLY (another agent will replace it): a Card titled \"Analyse Claude\" with sections placeholder; if book.summary/analysis exist display them with react-markdown; else a disabled Button \"Analyse Claude\" with caption \"Bientôt disponible\". Keep the props interface: { book: Book; author: Author }.\n- src/app/livres/nouveau/page.tsx and src/app/livres/[id]/modifier/page.tsx — thin server components loading authors (listAuthors()) and (for modifier) the book, rendering:\n- src/components/books/book-form.tsx — client component, react-hook-form + zodResolver (@hookform/resolvers/zod), fields: Titre (Input), Auteur (Combobox via Popover+Command searching authors accent-insensitively with normalizeKey; when no match, show a create option \"Créer l'auteur « X »\" which sets newAuthor:{name:X} and displays it as selected), Catégorie (Select, required), Genre (Input), Courant (Input), Thème (Input), Période (Select of PERIODS + \"—\"), Année de publication (number Input, accepts negative for av. J.-C.), Public (Select AUDIENCES, default adultes), Vision du monde (Select WORLDVIEWS showing WORLDVIEW_LABELS + option \"—\"), Langue originale (Input), Notes (Textarea). Submit POSTs/PUTs to the API, French toasts (\"Livre créé\", \"Livre mis à jour\", error toast with server {error}), then router.push to the detail page. Cancel button goes back.\n\n### C. Constraints\n- Your file namespace: src/app/api/books/**, src/app/livres/[id]/**, src/app/livres/nouveau/**, src/components/books/{book-form,delete-book-dialog,analysis-panel}.tsx. Another agent owns src/app/livres/page.tsx and src/components/books/book-table/filters/grouped/books-view — DO NOT create or modify those.\n- DO NOT modify: src/db/*, src/lib/*, layout, main-nav, package.json, next.config.ts, src/app/auteurs/** (another agent owns it — /auteurs/[id] links will resolve later).\n- react-markdown is installed. All needed shadcn ui components are in src/components/ui (add missing ones via `npx shadcn@latest add -y <name>` only if truly needed).\n- Verify: `cd /Users/tom/Documents/my-library/app && npx tsc --noEmit` zero errors. You MAY smoke-test the API by running `npm run dev -- --port 3103` briefly and curling POST/GET/PUT/DELETE against http://localhost:3103 (kill the server afterwards!). DO NOT run `npm run build`. Do not commit.\n\nReport back: files created, tsc result, curl smoke-test results if performed, deviations.","uuid":"33b21a74-7de2-4886-8288-aa507a12bb81","session_id":"893f4819-6d94-4f67-849d-3e57eeca4b35"}
